  icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 67d38cb932249a949bcffea63e951ee4, type: 3}
  rarity: 0
  itemType: 3
  description: '<b>JFK AND FDA GREENLIGHT CONTROVERSIAL URANIUM VACCINE</b>

    WASHINGTON
    D.C. Freshly elected President John F. Kennedy and the FDA announced today the
    unprecedented approval of a controversial serum containing trace uranium isotopes.

    "We
    must harness the atom to eradicate starvation," the newly inaugurated President
    declared Thursday, dubbing the serum a miracle.

    Developed with the Atomic
    Energy Commission, the vaccine''s microscopic radiation fundamentally alters
    human metabolism, providing endless cellular energy and permanently curing physical
    hunger without the need for traditional food.

    However, this bold move by
    the young administration has shocked scientists. Physicians warn against substituting
    natural digestion with atomic energy. FDA Commissioner George P. Larrick quickly
    dismissed these fears, stating the radiation dosage is less than a day in the
    summer sun.

    Despite White House backing, the public remains divided. While
    some hail the end of global poverty, anxious farmers and mothers have picketed
    the Capitol demanding natural food.

    Voluntary distribution begins late next
    month.'
